sycl: indexed bias and sinks in the MKL flash-attention path

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0013.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

An indexed bias kept attention on the SIMD tile kernel, whose bias path
cannot use its GQA layout. The MKL path (KQ GEMM, online softmax, V GEMM on
XMX, chunked over 8192 keys) now takes it: the softmax adds table[bin] to
the mask in F32, as the tile kernel does, and the normalization folds in the
sinks as the tile kernel's final scale does. Sinks without an indexed bias
keep their path. Inkling's attention at a 512-token ubatch, q8_0 K/V, GQA 3
on the Arc Pro B60 (measured on the earlier pin): 5.9 -> 5.5 ms at 1536 keys,
38.5 -> 12.1 ms at 10240 and 74.6 -> 20.3 ms at 20480.

